meta {
  name: link dev bob (navigation)
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

get {
  url: {{bff_url}}/api/auth/link?provider=dev&user=bob
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  The account page's "link another login" navigation, session-guarded
  (unlike /api/auth/login: with no cookie in the jar it answers 401).
  The dev provider links in one hop: the gateway answers 302 to
  /account?linked=dev with a re-sealed session cookie, and Bruno
  follows to the SPA shell (200). Outcomes travel as query params on
  the redirect: ?linked=dev on success, ?link_error=conflict when
  dev-bob already belongs to another account (linking never moves a
  login), ?link_error=link_failed otherwise. Real providers redirect
  to the provider's authorize URL instead and come back through
  /api/auth/callback.
}
